      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "6f5a3be6-ecd6-4712-b8aa-1c6cd9b8f2e7",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E4* hotel\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide on Days 3 \u0026amp; 4\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne free place per 10 paying passengers\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "d89f7476-6109-40dd-8184-7898d4835347",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on a half board basis at the 4* Park House Hotel in Shifnal in the heart of the beautiful Shropshire countryside. Facilities at the hotel include a restaurant and bar and all rooms are en suite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "ed6e65a4-6855-4163-b791-e6a1084f92b6",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECadbury\u2019s World\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIronbridge\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlists Hill Victorian Town\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWightwick Manor\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBarber Institute of Fine Arts\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStokesay Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELudlow\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESevern Valley Railway\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBridgnorth\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlack Country Living Museum\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "a45bfc82-4763-4513-ac3b-a8b36e2760a3",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHartlebury Castle - first given to Bishop Aelhun in 855AD, the Castle was the home of the Bishops of Worcester until 2007, and three of its bishops became saints, two were burned at the stake for their faith, one became the Pope who refused Henry the VIII his divorce\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWorld of Wedgwood - guided tour of the factory sees craftsmen at work, utilising unique artisan skills and techniques honed over 250 years\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGladstone Pottery Museum - the former Gladstone China Works is now preserved as the last complete Victorian pottery factory in the country\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "f0d59ad8-2b87-423b-8fd8-8594dea2f72e",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Cadbury\u2019s World\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 stop at Cadbury\u2019s World at Bourneville, dedicated to the history of chocolate \u2013 check in at the 4* Park House Hotel in Shifnal.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 Ironbridge \u0026amp; Blists Hill Victorian Town\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EIronbridge, the great symbol of the success of the iron industry, was cast in 1779 by Abraham Darby and its great arch enthralled visitors who came from all over the world to admire its construction, as they still do today \u2013 see the Ironbridge and Toll House and visit the Coalport China Museum and the Jackfield Tile Museum \u2013 Blists Hill Victorian Town is a recreation of life in a Victorian community with working factories, shops and cottages as well as the \u2018townsfolk\u2019.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 Wightwick Manor \u0026amp; the Barber Institute of Fine Arts\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWightwick Manor, one of only a few surviving examples of a house built and furnished under the influence of the Arts and Crafts Movement, contains many original William Morris wallpapers and fabrics, Pre-Raphaelite paintings and de Morgan ware \u2013 time at leisure in Birmingham and on an individual basis you may choose to enjoy a canal cruise \u2013 the Barber Institute of Fine Arts is home to a fine art collection by artists such as Monet, Manet, Renoir, Rubens, Rodin, and van Dyck.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 Stokesay Castle, Ludlow, Severn Valley Railway \u0026amp; Bridgnorth\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EEnglish Heritage\u2019s Stokesay Castle is a perfectly preserved medieval fortified manor house dating back to the 11th century and nestling in a green valley in the heart of the Shropshire countryside \u2013 time at leisure in Ludlow for lunch \u2013 one way 16 mile steam train excursion from Kidderminster to Bridgnorth on the Severn Valley Railway is a wonderful way to explore the beauty of the River Severn (those not opting for the train excursion continue by coach to Kidderminster) \u2013 remainder of the afternoon in the historic town of Bridgnorth.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 \u2013 Black Country Living Museum\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe award winning Black Country Living Museum, with period shops and houses set in a landscape of 26 acres, offers a glimpse into 300 years of history and reveals what it was like to live and work in one of the world\u2019s most industrialised landscapes.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "Remember this itinerary is just our suggestion. "
          }
        }
      ]
    },
